<title>KAZAKHSTAN: Kazakh 3-mth T-bill av yield rises to 22.52 pct.</title>
<headline>Kazakh 3-mth T-bill av yield rises to 22.52 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ALMATY 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on an issue of three-month GKO discount Treasury bills rose to 22.52 percent annual at an auction on Tuesday from 21.23 percent at the last auction on March 11, the National Bank said.</p>
<p>Details of the auction:</p>
<p>					   March 18	   March 11</p>
<p> Series number			 KZ43K1906975     KZ43K1206970</p>
<p> Issue volume (million tenge)	  650		  650</p>
<p> Bids (nominal, million tenge)	 780		  2,010</p>
<p> Sold (nominal, million tenge)	 650		  652</p>
<p> Average price			 94.67		94.96</p>
<p> Average yield			 22.52		21.23</p>
<p> Tenor				   91 days	    91 days</p>
<p> Maturity				June 19, 1997    June 12, 1997</p>
<p>--Almaty Newsroom, +7 3272 509410</p>
